    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **45 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `checkDigit` as a single Luhn check digit computed over the digits of the owner's `customerCode`, following the codebase's existing conventions for derived read-only fields.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `checkDigit` property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly `int32`, range 0\u20139), mirroring how other derived fields like `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel` are declared. This regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `checkDigit` field during the build.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` that populates `checkDigit` via `luhnCheckDigit(owner.getCustomerCode())`, and a `luhnCheckDigit` helper implementing the standard Luhn algorithm (last digit doubled first, non-digit characters like the hyphens in the code ignored, result `(10 - sum % 10) % 10`). This matches the reference `luhn(...)` in `AcceptanceBase` exactly, so the test's independent recomputation asserts the same value.\n\nThe new `Cp31Tests.coreCheckDigitIsLuhnOfCustomerCode` passes, and all 45 existing tests remain green.",
